From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: map each Rx ring to its own queues

The PPE RING_Q_MAP table holds one queue bitmap per EDMA ring, at
0x42a000 + 0x40 * ring_id, and records the set of PPE queues associated
with that ring.  edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_to_queue_mapping() writes the
same list, rx_queues[] = { 0, 8, 16, 24 }, into the entry of every Rx
ring, so each ring is given one queue from each of the four cores.

That disagrees with the QID2RID table the driver programs in
edma_cfg_rx_qid_to_rx_desc_ring_mapping(), which delivers unicast queue
q to ring ring_start + q / EDMA_MAX_PRI_PER_CORE.  A ring is therefore
associated with three queues that are never delivered to it, while seven
of the eight unicast queues that are delivered to it are left out of its
bitmap.  The driver's own log strings call this the ring's backpressure
configuration, and the sibling driver for the same block in this tree,
qualcommax qca_ppe_scheduler.c ppe_edma_ring_map_init(), programs
disjoint per-ring queue sets in the same table, so one list shared by
every ring is not the intended use.

Give each ring the queues that QID2RID routes to it, taken from
edma_rx_ring_queue_map[] which already describes that layout.  That
table has one column per ring, so bound the ring count by its width
where the ring count is already validated; the existing check there
bounds it by num_possible_cpus(), which is not the same thing, and
edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_reset_queue_priority() indexes the same table.

The first ring is also the target of the CPU port multicast queues.
Those are not in its bitmap before or after this change.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
@@ -92,7 +92,8 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_reset_q
 	struct edma_ring_info *rx = hw_info->rx;
 	u32 i, ret;
 
-	if (unlikely(rx->num_rings > num_possible_cpus())) {
+	if (unlikely(rx->num_rings > num_possible_cpus() ||
+		     rx->num_rings > ARRAY_SIZE(edma_rx_ring_queue_map[0]))) {
 		pr_err("Invalid count of rxdesc rings: %d\n",
 		       rx->num_rings);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -127,13 +128,18 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_to_queu
 
 	/* Rxdesc ring to PPE queue mapping */
 	for (i = 0; i < rx->num_rings; i++) {
+		int queues[ARRAY_SIZE(edma_rx_ring_queue_map)];
 		struct edma_rxdesc_ring *rxdesc_ring;
+		u32 pri;
 
 		rxdesc_ring = &edma_ctx->rx_rings[i];
 
+		for (pri = 0; pri < ARRAY_SIZE(queues); pri++)
+			queues[pri] = edma_rx_ring_queue_map[pri][i];
+
 		ret = ppe_edma_ring_to_queues_config(edma_ctx->ppe_dev,
 						     rxdesc_ring->ring_id,
-						ARRAY_SIZE(rx_queues), rx_queues);
+						     ARRAY_SIZE(queues), queues);
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in configuring Rx ring to PPE queue mapping, ret: %d, id: %d\n",
 			       ret, rxdesc_ring->ring_id);
